\item \points{7b}

For this and next question, imagine you are choosing between two proof-based systems. 
System A is sound but not complete. System B is complete but not sound. 
Assume the only difference between System A and System B is the difference between soundness and completeness.

You want to deploy one of these systems in a safety-critical setting, where acting on a false conclusion has severe consequences. Which system would you choose and why? 

\textbf{What we expect:} 2-3 sentences explaining your choice, tying in the definitions of soundness and completeness. 

